              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the German for to be true, then the German for to turn out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: zusagen",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zusagen — \"to accept (an invitation), to promise; to appeal to\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sie hat für die Hochzeit zugesagt. She has accepted the invitation to the wedding."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Separable: sie sagt zu, sie hat zugesagt. Das sagt mir zu — I like that."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zusagen is built from zu and sagen \"to say\", inherited from Proto-Germanic sagjaną (EtymDB), a cousin of English say: you say yes to something."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
